# Zig Source Rules

## Memory

- Stack by default. Heap via `allocator.create`, `.alloc`, `ArrayList`, `ArenaAllocator`.
- `defer` runs LIFO on **every** scope exit (success, error, break). `errdefer` runs only on error exit from current block.
- Long-lived owned data: caller allocates or document transfer. Use `ArenaAllocator` for batch free.

## Errors

- `if (result) |val| { } else |err| { }` — capture required on error branch.
- `@errorReturnTrace()` for programmatic trace; enabled Debug/ReleaseSafe.
- Narrow error sets at API boundaries; merge with `A || B` for platform branches.

## Comptime

- `comptime` params must be known at call site. `@TypeOf`, `@typeInfo`, `@sizeOf` for reflection.
- `inline while` / `inline for` unroll at compile time when index is comptime-known.

## C interop

- Match C ABI: `[*c]T` for unknown mutability; prefer `[*]T` / `*T` after review.
- `@export` / `export` for Zig→C. `linkSystemLibrary("foo")` in `build.zig`.
